🚀 Installation and Setup

Prerequisites

- Node.js 18 or later
- npm
- PostgreSQL
- Git
- Visual Studio Code (recommended)

Step 1: Clone the Repository

git clone https://github.com/krishna-k-sah/Local-Events-Calendar.git
cd Local-Events-Calendar

Step 2: Install Backend Dependencies

cd server
npm install

Step 3: Configure Environment Variables

Create a ".env" file inside the "server" directory.

Configure your database connection and authentication settings using the project's environment configuration.

Step 4: Set Up Database

Configure PostgreSQL and apply the database migrations:

npx prisma migrate deploy --schema=prisma/schema.postgresql.prisma
npm run prisma:seed

Step 5: Start Backend

npm run dev

Backend runs on:

"http://localhost:5000"

Step 6: Install and Start Frontend

Open another terminal:

cd client
npm install
npm run dev

Frontend runs on:

"http://localhost:5173"

🧪 Testing

Run backend tests:

npm run test:server

Build the frontend:

npm run build

🎯 Project Objectives

1. Make local event discovery easier.
2. Provide a centralized event management platform.
3. Simplify event registration and digital ticketing.
4. Improve communication between organizers and attendees.
5. Provide an organized and interactive event calendar.

🔮 Future Improvements

- Mobile application integration.
